<https://sanskrit-lexicon.github.io/csl-standards/registers/small-class-2006#unresolved-GL.> a scr:UnresolvedForm ;
  skos:notation "GL."^^<https://sanskrit-lexicon.github.io/csl-standards/registers/small-class-2006#AbbreviationNotation> ;
  scr:smallClass <https://sanskrit-lexicon.github.io/csl-standards/registers/small-class-2006#2006-1> ;
  scr:paperQuote "combinations involving cases (without the dot sign to economize space) as IDAbl., NA. and GL. (Kn)"@en ;
  scr:reason "Combination form; no census legend carries it. Components G. and L. are register concepts, but the combination itself is unattested in the census."@en ;
  scr:externalGrounding [ scr:source "Whitney 1879" ; scr:edition "A Sanskrit Grammar, 2nd ed. 1889 (Leipzig/Boston; the paper's reference is Whitney 2004/1879, New Delhi); quotes from the estate digitization gasyoun/SanskritGrammar WhitneyGrammar_1889 (English Wikisource text)" ; scr:quote "G. L. कामयोस् kā́mayos देवयोस् deváyos आस्ययोस् āsyàyos" ; scr:locator "§330 (dual)" ] ,
      [ scr:source "Whitney 1879" ; scr:edition "A Sanskrit Grammar, 2nd ed. 1889 (Leipzig/Boston; the paper's reference is Whitney 2004/1879, New Delhi); quotes from the estate digitization gasyoun/SanskritGrammar WhitneyGrammar_1889 (English Wikisource text)" ; scr:quote "I. D. Ab. dvā́bhyām; G. L. dváyos." ; scr:locator "§482 d" ] .

<https://sanskrit-lexicon.github.io/csl-standards/registers/small-class-2006#unresolved-IDAbl.> a scr:UnresolvedForm ;
  skos:notation "IDAbl."^^<https://sanskrit-lexicon.github.io/csl-standards/registers/small-class-2006#AbbreviationNotation> ;
  scr:smallClass <https://sanskrit-lexicon.github.io/csl-standards/registers/small-class-2006#2006-1> ;
  scr:paperQuote "combinations involving cases (without the dot sign to economize space) as IDAbl., NA. and GL. (Kn)"@en ;
  scr:reason "Combination form; no census legend carries it, and the component cases (instrumental, dative, ablative) are not individually proposed in the source's one-letter row."@en ;
  scr:externalGrounding [ scr:source "Knauer" ; scr:edition "Učebnik' sanskritskago jazyka, Leipzig, 1908; apparatus of the 2021 Bibliotheca Sanscritica digitization gasyoun/SanskritGrammar BibliothecaSanscritica/KnauerUchebnik_2021" ; scr:quote "у Кнауэра может быть часть «поезда» IDAblL., единственная аббревиатура, которую нельзя сократить до одной буквы, ибо тогда сольется с accusativus" ; scr:locator "apparatus note on Abl. (2021 digitization)" ] ,
      [ scr:source "Whitney 1879" ; scr:edition "A Sanskrit Grammar, 2nd ed. 1889 (Leipzig/Boston; the paper's reference is Whitney 2004/1879, New Delhi); quotes from the estate digitization gasyoun/SanskritGrammar WhitneyGrammar_1889 (English Wikisource text)" ; scr:quote "I. D. Ab. कामाभ्याम् kā́mābhyām देवाभ्याम् devā́bhyām आस्याभ्याम् āsyā̀bhyām" ; scr:locator "§330 (dual)" ] .

<https://sanskrit-lexicon.github.io/csl-standards/registers/small-class-2006#unresolved-Inj.> a scr:UnresolvedForm ;
  skos:notation "Inj."^^<https://sanskrit-lexicon.github.io/csl-standards/registers/small-class-2006#AbbreviationNotation> ;
  scr:smallClass <https://sanskrit-lexicon.github.io/csl-standards/registers/small-class-2006#2006-3> ;
  scr:paperQuote "moods Inj., Ipv., Ipf, Ppf., Prc, Gdv., Inf., in small caps (Mc)"@en ;
  scr:reason "No census legend carries the form, and the expansion (injunctive) is not stated in the source. Registering a concept would assign a sense the census does not evidence."@en ;
  scr:externalGrounding [ scr:source "Macdonell 1916" ; scr:edition "A Vedic Grammar for Students, Oxford: Clarendon Press, 1916; scans archive.org in.ernet.dli.2015.531262 and dli.csl.8570 (OCR, tokens noted where garbled)" ; scr:quote "indec., indeclinable. inf., infinitive. inj., injunctive," ; scr:locator "List of Abbreviations" ] ,
      [ scr:source "Macdonell 1916" ; scr:edition "A Vedic Grammar for Students, Oxford: Clarendon Press, 1916; scans archive.org in.ernet.dli.2015.531262 and dli.csl.8570 (OCR, tokens noted where garbled)" ; scr:quote "Besides the indicative there are four moods, the subjunctive, the injunctive, the optative, and the imperative, all of which are formed from the stems of the present, the perfect, and the aorist." ; scr:locator "§122 a" ] .

<https://sanskrit-lexicon.github.io/csl-standards/registers/small-class-2006#unresolved-NA.> a scr:UnresolvedForm ;
  skos:notation "NA."^^<https://sanskrit-lexicon.github.io/csl-standards/registers/small-class-2006#AbbreviationNotation> ;
  scr:smallClass <https://sanskrit-lexicon.github.io/csl-standards/registers/small-class-2006#2006-1> ;
  scr:paperQuote "combinations involving cases (without the dot sign to economize space) as IDAbl., NA. and GL. (Kn)"@en ;
  scr:reason "Combination form; no census legend carries it, and the component cases it combines (nominative + accusative) are not all individually proposed in the source's one-letter row (N. G. L. only)."@en ;
  scr:externalGrounding [ scr:source "Whitney 1879" ; scr:edition "A Sanskrit Grammar, 2nd ed. 1889 (Leipzig/Boston; the paper's reference is Whitney 2004/1879, New Delhi); quotes from the estate digitization gasyoun/SanskritGrammar WhitneyGrammar_1889 (English Wikisource text)" ; scr:quote "Dva two is dual only, and is entirely regular: thus, N. A. V. dvāú (dvā́, Veda) m., dvé f. n.; I. D. Ab. dvā́bhyām; G. L. dváyos." ; scr:locator "§482 d" ] ,
      [ scr:source "Whitney 1879" ; scr:edition "A Sanskrit Grammar, 2nd ed. 1889 (Leipzig/Boston; the paper's reference is Whitney 2004/1879, New Delhi); quotes from the estate digitization gasyoun/SanskritGrammar WhitneyGrammar_1889 (English Wikisource text)" ; scr:quote "Dual: N. A. V. कामौ kā́māu देवौ devāú आस्ये āsyè I. D. Ab. कामाभ्याम् kā́mābhyām देवाभ्याम् devā́bhyām आस्याभ्याम् āsyā̀bhyām G. L. कामयोस् kā́mayos देवयोस् deváyos आस्ययोस् āsyàyos" ; scr:locator "§330" ] .

<https://sanskrit-lexicon.github.io/csl-standards/registers/small-class-2006#unresolved-pfph.> a scr:UnresolvedForm ;
  skos:notation "pfph."^^<https://sanskrit-lexicon.github.io/csl-standards/registers/small-class-2006#AbbreviationNotation> ;
  scr:smallClass <https://sanskrit-lexicon.github.io/csl-standards/registers/small-class-2006#2006-4> ;
  scr:paperQuote "participium ppfa. pfph."@en ;
  scr:reason "No census legend carries the form, and the source states no expansion."@en ;
  scr:externalGrounding [ scr:source "Whitney 1879" ; scr:edition "A Sanskrit Grammar, 2nd ed. 1889 (Leipzig/Boston; the paper's reference is Whitney 2004/1879, New Delhi); quotes from the estate digitization gasyoun/SanskritGrammar WhitneyGrammar_1889 (English Wikisource text)" ; scr:quote "Hence they are, like more proper participles, sometimes treated as a part of the general verbal system, and called future passive participles, or gerundives (like the Latin forms in ndus, to which they correspond in meaning)." ; scr:locator "§961" ] .

<https://sanskrit-lexicon.github.io/csl-standards/registers/small-class-2006#unresolved-pn.> a scr:UnresolvedForm ;
  skos:notation "pn."^^<https://sanskrit-lexicon.github.io/csl-standards/registers/small-class-2006#AbbreviationNotation> ;
  scr:smallClass <https://sanskrit-lexicon.github.io/csl-standards/registers/small-class-2006#2006-2> ;
  scr:paperQuote "participium pp. pn."@en ;
  scr:reason "The source gives no expansion for pn.; the census's only pn. legend reads 'pronoun, pronominal.' (MD), which contradicts a participle reading. Left unresolved rather than bound against the evidence."@en ;
  scr:censusConflict "pn. legend: [MD] 'pronoun, pronominal.'"@en ;
  scr:externalGrounding [ scr:source "Whitney 1879" ; scr:edition "A Sanskrit Grammar, 2nd ed. 1889 (Leipzig/Boston; the paper's reference is Whitney 2004/1879, New Delhi); quotes from the estate digitization gasyoun/SanskritGrammar WhitneyGrammar_1889 (English Wikisource text)" ; scr:quote "The pronouns differ from the great mass of nouns and adjectives chiefly in that they come by derivation from another and a very limited set of roots, the so-called pronominal or demonstrative roots." ; scr:locator "§490" ] .

<https://sanskrit-lexicon.github.io/csl-standards/registers/small-class-2006#unresolved-ppfa.> a scr:UnresolvedForm ;
  skos:notation "ppfa."^^<https://sanskrit-lexicon.github.io/csl-standards/registers/small-class-2006#AbbreviationNotation> ;
  scr:smallClass <https://sanskrit-lexicon.github.io/csl-standards/registers/small-class-2006#2006-4> ;
  scr:paperQuote "participium ppfa. pfph."@en ;
  scr:reason "No census legend carries the form, and the source states no expansion."@en ;
  scr:externalGrounding [ scr:source "Whitney 1879" ; scr:edition "A Sanskrit Grammar, 2nd ed. 1889 (Leipzig/Boston; the paper's reference is Whitney 2004/1879, New Delhi); quotes from the estate digitization gasyoun/SanskritGrammar WhitneyGrammar_1889 (English Wikisource text)" ; scr:quote "It consists in a derivative nomen agentis, having the value of a future active participle, and used, either with or without an accompanying auxiliary, in the office of a verbal tense with future meaning." ; scr:locator "§942 b" ] .

<https://sanskrit-lexicon.github.io/csl-standards/registers/small-class-2006#unresolved-Prc> a scr:UnresolvedForm ;
  skos:notation "Prc"^^<https://sanskrit-lexicon.github.io/csl-standards/registers/small-class-2006#AbbreviationNotation> ;
  scr:smallClass <https://sanskrit-lexicon.github.io/csl-standards/registers/small-class-2006#2006-3> ;
  scr:paperQuote "moods Inj., Ipv., Ipf, Ppf., Prc, Gdv., Inf., in small caps (Mc)"@en ;
  scr:reason "No census legend carries the form, and the source states no expansion. Left unresolved rather than guessed."@en ;
  scr:externalGrounding [ scr:source "Macdonell 1916" ; scr:edition "A Vedic Grammar for Students, Oxford: Clarendon Press, 1916; scans archive.org in.ernet.dli.2015.531262 and dli.csl.8570 (OCR, tokens noted where garbled)" ; scr:quote "Pluperfect (ppf.) ; Aorist (ao.) ; Precative (prc.) ;" ; scr:locator "Appendix I (List of Verbs), order of the parts" ] ,
